---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '@/lib/data';
---

<BaseLayout title="About the sample registry · NameFrame" description="Why NameFrame publishes a separate repository for inspectable synthetic-data outputs.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={withBase('/')}>Home</a><span>/</span><span>About</span></nav>
    <p class="kicker">About this repository</p>
    <h1>A public window into the outputs.</h1>
    <p class="lede">This repository exists so teams can inspect examples without exposing the proprietary product that generated them.</p>
  </header>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="content-grid">
      <article class="prose">
        <h2>What NameFrame is</h2>
        <p>NameFrame is an Unreal-native synthetic-data studio for generating computer-vision datasets with aligned visual modalities, derived annotations and validation evidence.</p>
        <h2>Why a companion repository</h2>
        <p>Product source, engine integration and internal pipeline details have a different security and licensing boundary from sample outputs. Separating them keeps the public material useful and the product boundary unambiguous.</p>
        <h2>What you can evaluate</h2>
        <p>Use the published previews, representative annotations, metadata, hashes and limitations to assess output structure and whether a scoped pilot is worth discussing.</p>
        <h2>What you cannot infer</h2>
        <p>A small public sample is not a benchmark, a production SLA, an open-source release or proof that synthetic data will improve a particular model.</p>
      </article>
      <aside class="panel side-facts"><h3>Next step</h3><p>If the outputs are relevant to your use case, describe the target classes, scene, modalities and evaluation plan in a pilot request.</p><a class="button" href="https://getnameframe.com/pilot">Apply for a pilot</a></aside>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="brand-heading">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Official identity</p>
        <h2 id="brand-heading">Frame the world. Name the frames.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>The mark, wordmark and visual symbols below are the official NameFrame brand assets used by the product and this public sample registry.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="brand-showcase">
      <img
        src={withBase('/brand/nameframe-brand-sheet.webp')}
        width="1600"
        height="900"
        alt="Official NameFrame brand sheet with the frame-and-cube mark, black and pink wordmark, and symbols for frame, world, focus and synthetic data"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption>Official light-background brand system. The public site uses the same black, white and NameFrame pink identity as the product.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
